    {
      "id": "d1947e4b41efc3af65eed4bc57b69eaa34e8fe83",
      "individual_note": false,
      "resolvable": true,
      "resolved": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2903381183,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "What's the motivation behind disabling all of these heuristic dissectors?  This one at least looks like it has enough of a \"magic number\" to qualify for a \"strong\" heuristic.",
          "author": {
            "id": 8399509,
            "username": "mmann78",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Michael Mann",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/fad119898ba16a3f8be2f765dcff399098444abd4f85a04d4c3ef415a2bbe3d9?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/mmann78"
          },
          "created_at": "2025-11-20T18:37:47.872Z",
          "updated_at": "2025-11-20T19:15:31.046Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 434115740,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": false,
          "resolved_by": null,
          "resolved_at": null,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 22383,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 2903467860,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "There's a \"cost\" for every heuristic disector being tried for every\nunclaimed packet even if the heurustic is strong. The rationale is if it is\nuncommon protocol let the ones needing it activly enable the heuristic.\n\nMaybe I'm the only one thinking this is a good idea and should stop making\nthe changes.\n\nskrev:",
          "author": {
            "id": 6792385,
            "username": "AndersBroman",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "AndersBroman",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/132fb48f26018ea9516aea909144af3c3a94eaf2ba477efaa9a232abe80d322c?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/AndersBroman"
          },
          "created_at": "2025-11-20T19:15:30.974Z",
          "updated_at": "2025-11-20T19:15:30.974Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 434115740,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": false,
          "resolved_by": null,
          "resolved_at": null,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 22383,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 2903648446,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "I don't know how to determine \"uncommon\" vs \"common\", but I don't want to have to handle bug reports of \"this used to work (for my niche protocol) ...\".  Also, I believe dissector documentation encourages heuristics if there isn't an IANA registered protocol.  And if I submit an \"uncommon\" new dissector tomorrow, will it be switched to \"disabled\" in a year or two because it wasn't \"popular\" enough?\nBut you're correct that the number of dissectors has grown to the point where we should start to consider \"pruning\". Or maybe there is an \"architectural\" change we can make to optimize \"common heuristic checks\" (like a magic number).",
          "author": {
            "id": 8399509,
            "username": "mmann78",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Michael Mann",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/fad119898ba16a3f8be2f765dcff399098444abd4f85a04d4c3ef415a2bbe3d9?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/mmann78"
          },
          "created_at": "2025-11-20T20:39:39.997Z",
          "updated_at": "2025-11-20T20:39:39.997Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 434115740,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": false,
          "resolved_by": null,
          "resolved_at": null,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 22383,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 2903799853,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "It's only the default being changed. Nothing is stoping any one from\nenabling them again. If default on is prefered lets turn them all on.\n\nskrev:",
          "author": {
            "id": 6792385,
            "username": "AndersBroman",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "AndersBroman",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/132fb48f26018ea9516aea909144af3c3a94eaf2ba477efaa9a232abe80d322c?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/AndersBroman"
          },
          "created_at": "2025-11-20T21:44:24.427Z",
          "updated_at": "2025-11-20T21:44:24.427Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 434115740,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": false,
          "resolved_by": null,
          "resolved_at": null,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 22383,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    }
